---
source: crates/kagebunshin/src/cli/mod.rs
expression: sub.clone().render_help().to_string()
---
Find names or keys that contain TEXT, ignoring case (never values)

Usage: kagebunshin search [OPTIONS] <TEXT>

Arguments:
  <TEXT>  What to look for, e.g. stripe

Options:
      --json                 Print machine-readable JSON; errors go to stderr as JSON
      --provider <PROVIDER>  Only this provider [possible values: aws_sm, file, proton]
      --prefix <PREFIX>      Only names that start with this
      --socket <PATH>        Daemon socket [default: $KAGEBUNSHIN_SOCKET, else a per-user runtime dir]
      --env <ENV>            Environment to use instead of the project's default
      --keys                 Also match AWS secrets' key names, which reads every AWS secret under the prefix (see `list --keys`)
      --profile <PROFILE>    The AWS profile [default: the one this checkout's project reads AWS with, else `[aws]` in config.toml, else the ambient configuration]
      --project <NAME>       Project to use instead of the one for this folder; it must claim this checkout's remotes
      --region <REGION>      The AWS region [default: this checkout's project's, else `[aws]` in config.toml, else the profile's]
  -h, --help                 Print help
  -V, --version              Print version
